-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.17 תוספת שהייה
-- The stay hours (שעות שהייה) of the collective agreement of 26.5.1981: who
-- must stay, for how many weekly hours by position share, how the hours are
-- scheduled and used, how they are planned and reported, and the 10% stay
-- supplement paid for them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.17 תוספת שהייה`

-- Rounding up to a whole number, for "on every quarter position or part of it".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rounded up` x IS
    IF TRUNC x 0 EQUALS x
    THEN x
    ELSE TRUNC x 0 PLUS 1

-- Section 1.17's own actors: the pedagogical council is not a party of the
-- takanon's shared vocabulary, so the section declares it here and wraps the
-- shared parties.
DECLARE `1.17 party` IS ONE OF
    `the pedagogical council`
    `a takanon party` HAS `who acts` IS A Party

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17/p7 The page's table of contents: the titles of the subsections below.

§§ `1.17.0 הקדמה`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0/p1 The introduction: the agreement of 26 May 1981 was signed, and what follows are its main points. It states no rule.

-- 1.17.0 ¶1: the agreement applies to these roles, when the agreements of
-- 25.8.1980 apply to them, except teaching employees in administrative posts.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0__para_1
DECLARE `teaching role` IS ONE OF
    `kindergarten teacher`
    `teacher`
    `professional instructor`
    `Shelach instructor`
    `principal`
    `teacher in a guidance role`
    `supervisor in an instructor grade`
    `supervisor`
    `another role`

GIVEN r IS A `teaching role`, `covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980` IS A BOOLEAN, `in an administrative post` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stay-hours agreement applies to` r `covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980` `in an administrative post` IF
        NOT r EQUALS `another role`
    AND `covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980`
    AND NOT `in an administrative post`

#ASSERT `the stay-hours agreement applies to` `kindergarten teacher` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the stay-hours agreement applies to` `teacher` TRUE TRUE

-- F-1.17-g: "עליהם חלים ההסכמים הקיבוציים מיום 25.8.1980" follows the last
-- role in the list ("ומפקחים"). Read as qualifying every role — the reading
-- adopted above — the agreement reaches only employees under the 1980
-- agreements; read as qualifying the supervisors alone, it reaches every
-- kindergarten teacher, teacher, instructor and principal.
GIVEN r IS A `teaching role`, `covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980` IS A BOOLEAN, `in an administrative post` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement applies, the 1980 clause qualifying supervisors only` r `covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980` `in an administrative post` IF
        NOT r EQUALS `another role`
    AND (`covered by the agreements of 25.8.1980` OR NOT r EQUALS `supervisor`)
    AND NOT `in an administrative post`

`the 1980 clause's reach changes who must stay` MEANS
    NOT (`the stay-hours agreement applies to` `teacher` FALSE FALSE
         EQUALS `the agreement applies, the 1980 clause qualifying supervisors only` `teacher` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the 1980 clause's reach changes who must stay`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_0/p5 The introduction's source list (אסמכתא): three Director-General's circulars.

§§ `1.17.1 שעות שהייה — the weekly hours`

-- ¶1: a full position stays two weekly hours in addition to the position's
-- hours, without changing how many hours a position is. The explanation's
-- 1ב repeats it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_1__subpara_b
`weekly stay hours of a full position` MEANS 2

GIVEN `hours of the position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours a position is, under the agreements` `hours of the position` IS
    `hours of the position`

GIVEN `hours of the position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly hours at the institution in a full position` `hours of the position` IS
    `the hours a position is, under the agreements` `hours of the position` PLUS `weekly stay hours of a full position`

-- ¶2: part-time employees stay in proportion to their position, "as
-- follows" — by 2א up to a third of a position, by 2ב above it. The rule
-- below is that proportion, for a share of one position or less at ONE
-- employer. At a full position (share 1) 2ב gives four quarters, two hours:
-- ¶1 agrees.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours up to one position` share IS
    BRANCH IF share AT MOST 0                   THEN 0
           IF share AT MOST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)    THEN `stay hours up to a third of a position` share
           OTHERWISE `stay hours above a third of a position` share

GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a part-time position` share IF
    share GREATER THAN 0 AND share LESS THAN 1

#ASSERT `stay hours up to one position` 1 EQUALS `weekly stay hours of a full position`
#ASSERT `stay hours up to one position` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `stay hours up to one position` 0.5 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `stay hours up to one position` 0.75 EQUALS 1.5

-- 2א: up to and including 1/3 of a position at one employer, half an hour.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours up to a third of a position` share IS 0.5

-- 2ב: more than 1/3, half an hour for every quarter position or part of it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours above a third of a position` share IS
    0.5 TIMES `rounded up` (share DIVIDED BY 0.25)

§§ `1.17.1 — above a full position (the explanation's 3)`

-- Explanation 3: above a full position the employee stays "in proportion to
-- the position", with an example: a post-primary full position of 24 hours,
-- worked at 25 to 32 hours, stays 2½ hours. The text gives no formula, and
-- the formula the part-time clause gives does not reproduce the example
-- (F-1.17-b). The reading adopted: the full position's two hours, plus the
-- part-time clause applied to the share ABOVE the full position. It is the
-- reading under which every hour of the example's band gives 2½.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_3/p1
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER @desc the position share worked, above one full position
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours above a full position` share IS
    `weekly stay hours of a full position` PLUS `stay hours up to one position` (`the share above a full position` share)

GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share above a full position` share IS
    share MINUS 1

-- The text's example: a post-primary teacher whose full position is 24
-- hours, working 25 to 32 hours, stays 2½ hours — every hour of the band
-- gives 2½ under the reading.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_3/p2
`a 24-hour position worked at 25 to 32 hours stays 2½ hours` MEANS
    all (GIVEN h YIELD `stay hours at 24-hour full position` h EQUALS 2.5) `the example's band of hours`

`the example's band of hours` MEANS LIST 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32

GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours at 24-hour full position` `hours worked` IS
    `stay hours above a full position` (`hours worked` DIVIDED BY 24)

#ASSERT `a 24-hour position worked at 25 to 32 hours stays 2½ hours`

-- F-1.17-b: the part-time clause's own rule (half an hour per quarter
-- position or part of it) applied to the whole share gives 3 hours at 31 and
-- 32 hours, and a straight proportion (2 hours x share) gives neither 2½ nor
-- a constant over the band: "in proportion" is not one formula.
GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the quarter rule on the whole share` `hours worked` IS
    `stay hours above a third of a position` (`hours worked` DIVIDED BY 24)

`"in proportion to the position" does not give the example under the part-time rule` MEANS
        `the quarter rule on the whole share` 31 EQUALS 3
    AND `the quarter rule on the whole share` 32 EQUALS 3
    AND NOT (2 TIMES (25 DIVIDED BY 24)) EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `"in proportion to the position" does not give the example under the part-time rule`

§§ `1.17.1 2ג — several employers`

-- 2ג ¶1: with more than one employer, the additional stay is set by the
-- position share at EACH employer — so it is computed employer by employer.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p1
GIVEN `shares at each employer` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly stay hours` `shares at each employer` IS
    sum (map `stay hours at one employer` `shares at each employer`)

-- The stay at one employer, by the share there: up to a full position by
-- 2א–2ב, above it by explanation 3.
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours at one employer` share IS
    IF share AT MOST 1
    THEN `stay hours up to one position` share
    ELSE `stay hours above a full position` share

-- 2ג ¶2: the hours at the different employers are not added up to set the
-- stay — not even where two employers employ him in ONE institution, such as
-- a six-year post-primary school. Whether they share one institution changes
-- nothing.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN `shares at each employer` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the employers share one institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours without adding up the hours at the employers` `shares at each employer` `the employers share one institution` IS
    `weekly stay hours` `shares at each employer`

-- What adding the shares up would give — the computation the text forbids.
GIVEN `shares at each employer` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what adding the shares up would give` `shares at each employer` IS
    `stay hours at one employer` (sum `shares at each employer`)

-- Two employers at 0.3 each, even in one six-year school: half an hour at
-- each, one hour in all — not the hour and a half of an added-up 0.6.
#ASSERT `weekly stay hours` (LIST 0.3, 0.3) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `stay hours without adding up the hours at the employers` (LIST 0.3, 0.3) TRUE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `what adding the shares up would give` (LIST 0.3, 0.3) EQUALS 1.5

§§ `1.17.1 2ד–2ה — scheduling`

-- 2ד ¶1: a stay session is never shorter than one hour; where needed, the
-- two half-hours of two weeks are joined into one whole hour given once a
-- fortnight. Time is counted in hours.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d/p1
GIVEN `session length` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stay session is long enough` `session length` IF
    `session length` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `weekly stay hours owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `half-hours are joined into a fortnightly hour` `weekly stay hours owed` IF
    NOT TRUNC `weekly stay hours owed` 0 EQUALS `weekly stay hours owed`

-- Over a fortnight a half-hour week's hours always make whole sessions.
GIVEN `weekly stay hours owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours scheduled per fortnight` `weekly stay hours owed` IS
    2 TIMES `weekly stay hours owed`

#ASSERT `half-hours are joined into a fortnightly hour` 1.5
#ASSERT `stay hours scheduled per fortnight` 1.5 EQUALS 3

-- 2ד ¶2: the number of weekly free hours ("windows", "doors") stays as was
-- customary until now, and the stay hours are scheduled within it; an
-- employee with no free hours in the timetable, or who wants it, has them
-- scheduled as agreed with the institution's principal.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d/p2
GIVEN `has free hours in the timetable` IS A BOOLEAN, `wants another arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `where the stay hours go`
DECIDE `the stay hours are scheduled` `has free hours in the timetable` `wants another arrangement` IS
    IF `has free hours in the timetable` AND NOT `wants another arrangement`
    THEN `in the free hours of the timetable`
    ELSE `as agreed between the employee and the principal`

DECLARE `where the stay hours go` IS ONE OF
    `in the free hours of the timetable`
    `as agreed between the employee and the principal`

GIVEN `weekly free hours customary until now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly free hours with the stay hours` `weekly free hours customary until now` IS
    `weekly free hours customary until now`

-- 2ד ¶3: stay hours fall only on days the employee is in the teaching timetable.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d/p3
GIVEN `the employee teaches that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stay hours may be scheduled on the day` `the employee teaches that day` IF
    `the employee teaches that day`

-- 2ה: a teacher working in several institutions of one owner may have the
-- stay hours joined in one of them — with the teacher's consent.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e
GIVEN `the institutions have one owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the teacher consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stay hours may be joined in one institution` `the institutions have one owner` `the teacher consents` IF
    `the institutions have one owner` AND `the teacher consents`

§§ `1.17.1 3–6 — a duty, not a choice`

-- 3 ¶1: staying is a duty and depends on no one's consent — not the
-- employee's, the principal's or the employer's. The hours owed are computed
-- from the shares alone; consent is not an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_3/p1
DECLARE `stay-hours action` IS ONE OF
    `stay at the institution` HAS `hours stayed` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `shares at each employer` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `stay-hours action`
DECIDE `the weekly stay duty` `shares at each employer` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `stay at the institution` h
          PROVIDED h AT LEAST `weekly stay hours` `shares at each employer`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.1(3): staying is a duty, not subject to anyone's consent"

-- 3 ¶2: the teacher may not ask to reduce the quota; stay hours fall only by
-- reducing the position. A request changes nothing; a smaller share does.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_3/p2
GIVEN `share of the position` IS A NUMBER, `the teacher asked for a reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours after a request` `share of the position` `the teacher asked for a reduction` IS
    `stay hours at one employer` `share of the position`

#ASSERT `stay hours after a request` 1 TRUE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `stay hours after a request` 0.5 FALSE EQUALS 1

-- 4: the rights that come from actually staying are not harmed by an error
-- of the principal or by the principal's failure to record them, provided
-- the stay hours were entered in the teaching employees' attendance report
-- at the school, as usual.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_4
GIVEN `stayed in fact` IS A BOOLEAN, `the principal erred or did not record it` IS A BOOLEAN, `entered in the attendance report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rights from the stay are kept` `stayed in fact` `the principal erred or did not record it` `entered in the attendance report` IF
        `stayed in fact`
    AND (IF `the principal erred or did not record it` THEN `entered in the attendance report` ELSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `the rights from the stay are kept` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the rights from the stay are kept` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- 5 (and the procedure's 2א.1, which repeats it): the stay hours are part of
-- the employee's weekly timetable.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p140
GIVEN `weekly teaching hours` IS A NUMBER, `weekly stay hours owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the weekly timetable in hours` `weekly teaching hours` `weekly stay hours owed` IS
    `weekly teaching hours` PLUS `weekly stay hours owed`

-- 6: the stay hours, joined to the position's hours as an inseparable part
-- of them, are cut only in direct proportion to a general cut in position
-- hours, if one is made. (Its "סעיפים 2 ו-3 לעיל": F-1.17-a.)
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_1__para_6
GIVEN `weekly stay hours owed` IS A NUMBER, `general cut in position hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `stay hours after a general cut` `weekly stay hours owed` `general cut in position hours` IS
    `weekly stay hours owed` TIMES (1 MINUS `general cut in position hours`)

-- F-1.17-a: ¶6 points at "sections 2 and 3 above" for the stay hours joined
-- to a FULL or PART-TIME position. In the list as printed, the full position
-- is ¶1, part-time ¶2, and ¶3 is the duty clause. Read as the agreement's
-- own numbers (its §1 is the scope clause printed in 1.17.0), 2 and 3 are
-- full and part-time — which is also how the procedure's "סעיף 3 להסכם"
-- sends part-time supervisors to the part-time rule.
DECLARE `subject of a clause` IS ONE OF
    `the full-position hours`
    `the part-time hours`
    `the duty to stay`
    `rights despite the principal's error`
    `the weekly timetable`
    `the cut in stay hours`

DECLARE `printed clause` HAS
    `clause number`  IS A NUMBER
    `clause subject` IS A `subject of a clause`

`the clauses of 1.17.1 as printed` MEANS
    LIST `printed clause` 1 `the full-position hours`,
         `printed clause` 2 `the part-time hours`,
         `printed clause` 3 `the duty to stay`,
         `printed clause` 4 `rights despite the principal's error`,
         `printed clause` 5 `the weekly timetable`,
         `printed clause` 6 `the cut in stay hours`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `subject of a clause`
DECIDE `the clause numbered` n IS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `clause subject`)
        (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `clause number` EQUALS n) `the clauses of 1.17.1 as printed`)

`"clauses 2 and 3 above" do not name the full and part-time clauses as printed` MEANS
        `the clause numbered` 2 EQUALS LIST `the part-time hours`
    AND `the clause numbered` 3 EQUALS LIST `the duty to stay`
    AND `the clause numbered` 1 EQUALS LIST `the full-position hours`
#ASSERT `"clauses 2 and 3 above" do not name the full and part-time clauses as printed`

§§ `1.17.1 explanation 1 — a full position and its age reduction`

-- Explanation 1א ¶1: "one full position", as the 1978-80 wage agreement
-- defined it, is a unit of work measured in weekly teaching hours, set by
-- the level of the educational framework and/or the employee's age. The
-- table of those hours is not in the corpus text (¶2 is its label), so it is
-- an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_1__subpara_a/p1
GIVEN `level of the educational framework` IS A STRING,
      `age of the employee` IS A NUMBER,
      `the full-position table of the 1978-80 agreement` IS A FUNCTION FROM STRING AND NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `one full position in weekly teaching hours` `level of the educational framework` `age of the employee` `the full-position table of the 1978-80 agreement` IS
    `the full-position table of the 1978-80 agreement` `level of the educational framework` `age of the employee`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_1__subpara_a/p2 The label of the full-position table ("טבלת פירוט…"); the table itself is not in the corpus text, so its hours are an input.

-- Explanation 1א ¶3: at 50 the position base falls by 2 weekly hours, at 55
-- by 2 more, 4 in all.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_1__subpara_a/p3
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `age reduction in weekly hours` age IS
    BRANCH IF age AT LEAST 55 THEN 4
           IF age AT LEAST 50 THEN 2
           OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `hours of a full position before reduction` IS A NUMBER, age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reduced position base` `hours of a full position before reduction` age IS
    `hours of a full position before reduction` MINUS `age reduction in weekly hours` age

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_2__subpara_c Explanation 2's labels for part-time tables (up to 1/3, 1/2 and 3/4 of a position); the tables are not in the corpus text, and the part-time rule they illustrate is encoded at 1.17.1 2א–2ב above.

§§ `1.17.1 explanation 4 — the position base after a reduction`

-- Explanation 4א / 4ב: employees entitled to a reduction of 2 / of 4 weekly
-- hours (the age reduction of explanation 1).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b
DECLARE `base after a reduction` HAS
    `base level`           IS A `level taught`
    `base reduction hours` IS A NUMBER
    `printed base`         IS A NUMBER

-- The two levels 4א and 4ב distinguish.
DECLARE `level taught` IS ONE OF
    `grades 1 to 6 or kindergarten`
    `grade 7 and up`

-- The base the rows print for a level and a reduction.
GIVEN l IS A `level taught`, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the printed base for` l r IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `printed base`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD b's `base level` EQUALS l AND b's `base reduction hours` EQUALS r) `the printed bases`)

-- Explanation 4: an employee entitled to a reduction has, "for every matter,
-- including the stay hours", the base printed here. The rows as printed:
`the printed bases` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_a__cls_1
        `base after a reduction` `grades 1 to 6 or kindergarten` 2 28,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_a__cls_2/p1
        `base after a reduction` `grade 7 and up` 2 26,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b__cls_1
        `base after a reduction` `grades 1 to 6 or kindergarten` 4 26,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b__cls_2/p1
        `base after a reduction` `grade 7 and up` 4 20

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 The word "Example:" that introduces the worked example below.

-- The example: 16 hours + 3 homeroom hours, with a 2- or 4-hour reduction,
-- is a position of 19/22 or 19/20 "according to his classification under א
-- or ב". F-1.17-c: 4ב.2's 20 agrees, but under א the example's 22 is neither
-- base א prints (28, 26); it is the post-primary 24-hour position of
-- explanation 3 less 2 — explanation 1's age rule — where 4א.2 prints 26.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b__cls_2/p3
GIVEN `the example's reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc 2 (classified under א) or 4 (under ב)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the example's position share` `the example's reduction` IS
    (16 PLUS 3) DIVIDED BY `the example's base` `the example's reduction`

GIVEN `the example's reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the example's base` `the example's reduction` IS
    IF `the example's reduction` EQUALS 2
    THEN `the example's base under א`
    ELSE `the example's base under ב`

`the example's base under א` MEANS 22
`the example's base under ב` MEANS 20

#ASSERT `the example's position share` 2 EQUALS 19 DIVIDED BY 22
#ASSERT `the example's position share` 4 EQUALS 19 DIVIDED BY 20

`4א.2 and the worked example give different bases for grade 7 and up` MEANS
        `the printed base for` `grade 7 and up` 2 EQUALS LIST 26
    AND NOT elem `the example's base under א` (map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `printed base`) `the printed bases`)
    AND `the reduced position base` 24 50 EQUALS `the example's base under א`
    AND `the printed base for` `grade 7 and up` 4 EQUALS LIST `the example's base under ב`
#ASSERT `4א.2 and the worked example give different bases for grade 7 and up`

-- The reading adopted (F-1.17-c): for grade 7 and up with a 2-hour
-- reduction the base is 22, as the example, explanation 1's age rule and
-- the 4-hour row (24 less 4 = 20) all give; every other row as printed.
GIVEN l IS A `level taught`, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position base after a reduction` l r IS
    IF l EQUALS `grade 7 and up` AND r EQUALS 2
    THEN `the example's base under א`
    ELSE sum (`the printed base for` l r)

GIVEN `weekly hours worked` IS A NUMBER, l IS A `level taught`, r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share after a reduction` `weekly hours worked` l r IS
    `weekly hours worked` DIVIDED BY `the position base after a reduction` l r

#ASSERT `the position share after a reduction` 19 `grade 7 and up` 2 EQUALS 19 DIVIDED BY 22
#ASSERT `the position share after a reduction` 19 `grade 7 and up` 4 EQUALS 19 DIVIDED BY 20

§§ `1.17.1 explanation 5 — the kindergarten teacher's stay plan`

-- 5א: the kindergarten teacher chooses one of three ways.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_a
DECLARE `kindergarten stay plan` IS ONE OF
    `two stay hours a week after the working day or in the afternoon`
    `fifteen minutes at the end of every working day`
    `one afternoon stay hour and fifteen minutes on three days`

-- The reading adopted (F-1.17-d): each way the text offers discharges the
-- kindergarten teacher's weekly stay duty, whatever minutes it comes to;
-- the choice is hers.
GIVEN p IS A `kindergarten stay plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chosen way discharges the weekly stay` p IF TRUE

-- F-1.17-d: with a 60-minute hour the three ways give 120, 75 or 90, and
-- 105 minutes — they are not one duty. They agree with each other and with
-- the two weekly hours of 1.17.1(1) only if a stay hour is 45 minutes and the
-- kindergarten works six days. Neither is said.
`the kindergarten ways are equal only with an undefined 45-minute hour` MEANS
        NOT `weekly stay minutes under the plan` `one afternoon stay hour and fifteen minutes on three days` 60 6 EQUALS 2 TIMES 60
    AND NOT `weekly stay minutes under the plan` `fifteen minutes at the end of every working day` 60 6 EQUALS 2 TIMES 60
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD `weekly stay minutes under the plan` p 45 6 EQUALS 2 TIMES 45)
            (LIST `two stay hours a week after the working day or in the afternoon`,
                  `fifteen minutes at the end of every working day`,
                  `one afternoon stay hour and fifteen minutes on three days`)
#ASSERT `the kindergarten ways are equal only with an undefined 45-minute hour`

-- The minutes each way gives in a week, for a given length of a "stay
-- hour" and number of working days; the text fixes neither (F-1.17-d).
GIVEN p IS A `kindergarten stay plan`, `minutes in a stay hour` IS A NUMBER, `working days in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly stay minutes under the plan` p `minutes in a stay hour` `working days in the week` IS
    CONSIDER p
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_a__cls_1
    WHEN `two stay hours a week after the working day or in the afternoon`
        THEN 2 TIMES `minutes in a stay hour`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_a__cls_2
    WHEN `fifteen minutes at the end of every working day`
        THEN 15 TIMES `working days in the week`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_a__cls_3
    WHEN `one afternoon stay hour and fifteen minutes on three days`
        THEN `minutes in a stay hour` PLUS 3 TIMES 15

-- 5ב: at the beginning of the school year she tells the parents of the plan
-- of stay hours with parents. Time in school months (September = 1).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `telling the parents` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `tell the parents of the stay-hours plan`
    WITHIN `month number` September
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.1, explanation 5ב: the parents are told at the beginning of the school year"

DECLARE `kindergarten action` IS ONE OF
    `tell the parents of the stay-hours plan`
    `tell the supervisor of the stay-hours plan`

-- 5ג: she tells the supervisor of the plan (days, hours) she will hold in the
-- year. The text gives no date, so the duty carries no deadline here.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1__hc_2__para_5__subpara_c
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `kindergarten action`
DECIDE `telling the supervisor` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `tell the supervisor of the stay-hours plan`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_1/p6 Subsection 1.17.1's source list (אסמכתא): circulars and the conditions-of-service unit's circular of 13.11.81.

§§ `1.17.2 הוראות ביצוע — what the stay hours are for`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p2 Headings: "the content of the activity in the stay hours" and "א. general".

-- ¶3: the content is aimed at the two goals of the Etzioni committee's
-- recommendations as implemented on 23.12.1980.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p3
DECLARE `stay-hours goal` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p4
    `caring for weak pupils to prevent dropping out and ease moves between frameworks`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p5
    `ties with parents and community and pupils' volunteering for the community`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p6 Heading: "ב. ways to reach the goals".

-- ¶7: the goals are reached by deepening the work of the educational staff
-- and the support staff through a system of activities that are NOT in the
-- field of teaching, carried out within the stay hours, that help the
-- education system reach the goals.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p7
GIVEN `outside the field of teaching` IS A BOOLEAN, `carried out within the stay hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `helps reach the goals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an activity of the stay hours` `outside the field of teaching` `carried out within the stay hours` `helps reach the goals` IF
        `outside the field of teaching`
    AND `carried out within the stay hours`
    AND `helps reach the goals`

-- ¶8 (and the activity notes' 1, "in no case frontal teaching"): to remove
-- doubt, the stay hours are not used for substitution, other teaching work,
-- supervising pupils or remedial lessons, and do not take the place of
-- existing roles that were given standard hours and/or a role allowance.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p84
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `stay-use action`
DECIDE `no forbidden use of stay hours` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    SHANT `assign the stay hours to` u
          PROVIDED `a use the stay hours are not for` u
    LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.17.2: stay hours are not for substitution, teaching, supervision, remedial lessons or existing roles"

DECLARE `use of stay hours` IS ONE OF
    `a non-teaching activity toward the goals`
    `substitute teaching`
    `other teaching work`
    `supervising pupils`
    `remedial lessons`
    `an existing role that had standard hours or a role allowance`
    `frontal teaching`

GIVEN u IS A `use of stay hours`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a use the stay hours are not for` u IF
    NOT u EQUALS `a non-teaching activity toward the goals`

GIVEN u IS A `use of stay hours`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a permitted use of stay hours` u IF
    NOT `a use the stay hours are not for` u

DECLARE `stay-use action` IS ONE OF
    `assign the stay hours to` HAS `use assigned` IS A `use of stay hours`
    `require time beyond the agreed stay hours`

#TRACE `no forbidden use of stay hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `assign the stay hours to` `substitute teaching` AT 3
#TRACE `no forbidden use of stay hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `assign the stay hours to` `a non-teaching activity toward the goals` AT 3

-- ¶9: no employee is required to give the stay activities more time than the
-- agreement sets — but that does not take away from the duties the existing
-- collective agreements and arrangements put on the employee.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p9
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `stay-use action`
DECIDE `no extra time for stay activities` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `require time beyond the agreed stay hours`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.17.2: no time beyond the agreed stay hours may be required for stay activities"

GIVEN `a duty under the existing agreements and arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty still binds the employee` `a duty under the existing agreements and arrangements` IF
    `a duty under the existing agreements and arrangements`

§§ `1.17.2 ג–ד — the lists of activities`

DECLARE `stay-hours group` IS ONE OF
    `every teaching employee`
    `teachers`
    `kindergarten teachers`
    `rhythmics teachers`
    `physical-education teachers`
    `agricultural-farm teachers`

DECLARE `listed activity` HAS
    `what is done` IS A STRING
    `listed for`   IS A `stay-hours group`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p10 Heading: "ג. the list of activities".

-- ¶11–¶17: the agreement's own seven activities, for every teaching employee.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p11
`the agreement's list of activities` MEANS
    LIST
        `listed activity` "personal talks with single pupils and their parents" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p12
        `listed activity` "preparing learning material fitted to the class and its level" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p13
        `listed activity` "working meetings with social workers, truant officers, the youth division, diagnosticians and psychologists" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p14
        `listed activity` "helping organise pupils who tutor pupils" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p15
        `listed activity` "preparing a plan for pupils' community service" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p16
        `listed activity` "guiding pupils in service to others and society, following up social and volunteer work" `every teaching employee`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p17
        `listed activity` "organising the care of the school, its gardens and surroundings" `every teaching employee`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p19 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p20 Headings: "ד. the activity of the groups of teaching employees", the label of a table of activities that is not in the corpus text, and "(2) the activities and their description".

-- ¶21: the stay activities listed above (ג) can be carried out in different
-- ways; the follow-up committee's activities below are brought as EXAMPLES
-- and possibilities, and more will be published from time to time. So the
-- examples do not close the class: an activity is proper if it is a
-- non-teaching activity toward the goals (¶7–¶8) and is listed (above, or
-- below for the employee's group), or is another way of carrying out the
-- activities listed above, or is published later.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p21
GIVEN `group of the employee` IS A `stay-hours group`, `what is done` IS A STRING, `another way of carrying out a listed activity` IS A BOOLEAN, `published as an additional activity` IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A `use of stay hours`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a proper stay activity` `group of the employee` `what is done` `another way of carrying out a listed activity` `published as an additional activity` u IF
        `a permitted use of stay hours` u
    AND (   any (GIVEN a YIELD a's `what is done` EQUALS `what is done`
                           AND (a's `listed for` EQUALS `group of the employee` OR a's `listed for` EQUALS `every teaching employee`))
                (concat (LIST `the agreement's list of activities`, `the examples of activities`))
         OR `another way of carrying out a listed activity`
         OR `published as an additional activity`)

#ASSERT `a proper stay activity` `kindergarten teachers` "home visits to all the children" FALSE FALSE `a non-teaching activity toward the goals`
#ASSERT NOT `a proper stay activity` `teachers` "home visits to all the children" FALSE FALSE `a non-teaching activity toward the goals`
#ASSERT NOT `a proper stay activity` `teachers` "decorating the school" FALSE FALSE `frontal teaching`

-- ¶22: detailed descriptions of successful activities in the institutions
-- will be brought to the teaching employees "in the course of time" — a duty
-- with no date. The sentence is passive; the party here is the Ministry of
-- Education, which issues the takanon.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p22
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `publication action`
DECIDE `bringing the descriptions` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `bring descriptions of successful activities to the teachers`

DECLARE `publication action` IS ONE OF
    `bring descriptions of successful activities to the teachers`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p23 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p25 Headings: "two examples follow", "א. preparing learning material…", "1. defining the subject".

§§ `1.17.2 Example א — preparing learning material`

-- ¶26: defining the subject needs three concepts, defined in ¶27–¶29.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p26
DECLARE `learning-material concept` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p27
    `a curriculum` @desc the framework setting out the principles, aims and contents of teaching a subject
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p28
    `learning materials` @desc textbooks, workbooks, worksheets, learning games and audio-visual aids, all based on the curriculum
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p29
    `a teacher's guide` @desc widening and deepening of the subject, didactic proposals, and lists of sources

-- ¶30: curricula are prepared by committees; materials and teacher's guides
-- by many bodies, teams of teachers among them.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p30
GIVEN c IS A `learning-material concept`
GIVETH A `who prepares`
DECIDE `who prepares it` c IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a curriculum` THEN `committees of educators, subject experts and sometimes public representatives`
    OTHERWISE `ministry units, higher-education units, individuals, and teams of teachers or single teachers`

DECLARE `who prepares` IS ONE OF
    `committees of educators, subject experts and sometimes public representatives`
    `ministry units, higher-education units, individuals, and teams of teachers or single teachers`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p31 Heading: "2. proposals for action".

-- ¶32: it is PROPOSED that in the stay hours teams of teachers work, guided
-- by a subject coordinator or an instructor, on defined tasks, as listed; the
-- order the proposals are listed in is also their proposed order of priority.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p32
GIVEN `a team of teachers` IS A BOOLEAN, `guided by a subject coordinator or an instructor` IS A BOOLEAN, `on a defined task` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed way of working` `a team of teachers` `guided by a subject coordinator or an instructor` `on a defined task` IF
        `a team of teachers`
    AND `guided by a subject coordinator or an instructor`
    AND `on a defined task`

DECLARE `material proposal` HAS
    `proposal`           IS A STRING
    `needs the supervisor's prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN

`the proposals in order of priority` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p33
        `material proposal` "preparing learning materials, after studying the curriculum and the existing materials" FALSE,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p40
        `material proposal` "preparing learning material of a local character" FALSE,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p41
        `material proposal` "preparing proposals for teachers (a teacher's guide)" FALSE,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p42
        `material proposal` "examining the curricula themselves and their fit to local needs" TRUE

-- ¶42, last words: examining the curricula needs the prior approval of the
-- institution's supervisor, and the supervisor confers on it with the
-- curriculum centre.
GIVEN p IS A `material proposal`, `the supervisor approved in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposal may be carried out` p `the supervisor approved in advance` IF
    (NOT p's `needs the supervisor's prior approval`) OR `the supervisor approved in advance`

DECLARE `curriculum review action` IS ONE OF
    `confer with the curriculum centre on the review`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `curriculum review action`
DECIDE `the supervisor confers with the curriculum centre` IS
    PARTY `the supervisor`
    MUST  `confer with the curriculum centre on the review`

-- ¶33–¶39: studying the existing materials asks two questions (¶34: can the
-- curriculum be carried out with them? ¶35: do they fit the pupils?) and
-- leads to one of three conclusions (¶36 introduces them), each of which
-- names the state of the materials it follows from.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p34 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p36
GIVEN `materials exist` IS A BOOLEAN, `the curriculum can be carried out with them` IS A BOOLEAN, `they fit the pupils` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `conclusion about the materials`
DECIDE `the conclusion` `materials exist` `the curriculum can be carried out with them` `they fit the pupils` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `materials exist`                          THEN JUST `no materials exist and they must be prepared from the curriculum`
           IF NOT `the curriculum can be carried out with them` THEN JUST `the materials are not a whole system and must be added to`
           IF NOT `they fit the pupils`                      THEN JUST `the materials are whole but must be recomposed for the pupils`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `conclusion about the materials` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p37
    `the materials are not a whole system and must be added to`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p38
    `the materials are whole but must be recomposed for the pupils`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p39
    `no materials exist and they must be prepared from the curriculum`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p43 Heading: "3. advice and guidance".

-- ¶44: in תשמ"ב instructor-teachers work with the curriculum-writing teams at
-- the curriculum centre and may help the teams of teachers. The teams may
-- approach the instructors directly or through the institution's supervisor,
-- and may also write to the curriculum centre for advice — through the
-- supervisor.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p44
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `advice action`
DECIDE `seeking advice` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `seek advice by` route

DECLARE `advice route` IS ONE OF
    `approaching the instructors directly`
    `approaching the instructors through the supervisor`
    `writing to the curriculum centre through the supervisor`

DECLARE `advice action` IS ONE OF
    `seek advice by` HAS `advice route taken` IS AN `advice route`

§§ `1.17.2 Example ב — individual care for a neglected child`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p45 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p46 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p47 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p48 The example's heading and its background: why a neglected child needs a personal tie with an adult, and what the tie does for the teacher. Explanation, no rule.

-- ¶49: individual care "can be carried out in this way": a teacher takes
-- on the care of ONE pupil, on the teacher's or the staff's initiative,
-- preferably a pupil who is not the teacher's own; the teacher sets a plan of
-- individual care and meets the pupil at least once a week. The duties bind
-- a teacher who has taken a pupil on in this way. Time in weeks.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p49
GIVEN `the teacher took on a pupil in this way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `individual care action`
DECIDE `the care of the pupil taken on` `the teacher took on a pupil in this way` IS
    IF `the teacher took on a pupil in this way`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `set a plan of individual care`
         HENCE `the weekly meeting`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `individual care action`
DECIDE `the weekly meeting` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `meet the pupil`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE `the weekly meeting`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.2, example ב: the teacher meets the pupil at least once a week"

DECLARE `who initiates the care` IS ONE OF
    `the teacher`
    `the school's educational staff`

GIVEN `pupils taken on by the teacher` IS A NUMBER, `the pupil is the teacher's own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pairing the text prefers` `pupils taken on by the teacher` `the pupil is the teacher's own` IF
    `pupils taken on by the teacher` EQUALS 1 AND NOT `the pupil is the teacher's own`

DECLARE `individual care action` IS ONE OF
    `set a plan of individual care`
    `meet the pupil`
    `consult a professional`

#TRACE `the care of the pupil taken on` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `set a plan of individual care` AT 0
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `meet the pupil` AT 1
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `meet the pupil` AT 2

-- ¶50: the teacher may consult professionals (a teacher-counsellor, a
-- psychologist, a social worker, a truant officer and the like); in some
-- cases group guidance can be organised in the school for several teachers
-- doing similar work.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p50
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `individual care action`
DECIDE `consulting` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `consult a professional`

GIVEN `several teachers do similar work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `group guidance may be organised in the school` `several teachers do similar work` IF
    `several teachers do similar work`

§§ `1.17.2 (3)–(7) — the examples of activities by group`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p51 Heading: "(3) the teacher's activities".

`the examples of activities` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p52
        `listed activity` "\"adopting\" a pupil and helping with social and learning problems" `teachers`,
        `listed activity` "systematic talks and guidance for a struggling pupil" `teachers`,
        `listed activity` "guidance talks with pupils moving to another institution" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p53
        `listed activity` "care of a pupil on the edge of dropping out, with the interdisciplinary staff" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p54
        `listed activity` "guiding tutors sent to pupils in the teacher's class" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p55
        `listed activity` "guiding pupils acting as \"big brothers\"" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p56
        `listed activity` "an institutional teachers' workshop on dropping out" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p57
        `listed activity` "an institutional teachers' workshop on tutoring" `teachers`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p58
