-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p83 Heading: "notes" (to the teacher's activities).

-- Notes 2–4 define three of the listed activities. Note 2: an
-- "institutional workshop" is learning and preparing programmes for dealing
-- with a subject; it lasts a set period, after which its participants act on
-- the subjects learned and planned.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p85
GIVEN `learning and preparing programmes on a subject` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a set period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the participants then act on what was planned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as an institutional workshop` `learning and preparing programmes on a subject` `for a set period` `the participants then act on what was planned` IF
        `learning and preparing programmes on a subject`
    AND `for a set period`
    AND `the participants then act on what was planned`

-- Note 3: preparing learning material means material for the school, the
-- class or the teachers — never the teacher's ordinary preparation of lessons.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p86
GIVEN `for the school, class or teachers` IS A BOOLEAN, `ordinary preparation of own lessons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as preparing learning material` `for the school, class or teachers` `ordinary preparation of own lessons` IF
    `for the school, class or teachers` AND NOT `ordinary preparation of own lessons`

-- Note 4: meetings with parents are meetings the teacher initiates, on a plan
-- set in advance.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p87
GIVEN `initiated by the teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, `on a plan set in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as meetings with parents` `initiated by the teacher` `on a plan set in advance` IF
    `initiated by the teacher` AND `on a plan set in advance`

§§ `1.17.2 ה — planning the work`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p120 Heading: "ה. planning the work".

-- ¶121: the pedagogical council (the principal and the staff), guided by the
-- supervisor, decides which kinds of activity from the list of activities
-- the institution's teaching employees carry out, in view of the needs of its
-- pupils and its community. The text gives no date.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p121
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.17 party` `planning action`
DECIDE `the council decides the kinds of activity` IS
    PARTY `the pedagogical council`
    MUST  `decide, guided by the supervisor, the kinds of activity from the list, in view of the pupils' and community's needs`

DECLARE `planning action` IS ONE OF
    `decide, guided by the supervisor, the kinds of activity from the list, in view of the pupils' and community's needs`
    `discuss the plan of action`
    `review the execution and its lessons`
    `send the protocol to the supervisor`
    `discuss the protocol with the principal`
    `discuss the kindergarten plans with the kindergarten teachers`

-- ¶122: the council discusses how the stay programmes are run at least twice
-- a year — the plan of action at the start of the year, the execution and its
-- lessons at its end. Time in school months (September = 1).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p122
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.17 party` `planning action`
DECIDE `the council's two yearly discussions` IS
    PARTY `the pedagogical council`
    MUST  `discuss the plan of action`
    WITHIN `month number` September
    HENCE (PARTY `the pedagogical council`
           MUST  `review the execution and its lessons`
           WITHIN `month number` August
           LEST  BREACH BY `the pedagogical council` BECAUSE "section 1.17.2(ה)2: the execution is reviewed at the end of the year")
    LEST  BREACH BY `the pedagogical council` BECAUSE "section 1.17.2(ה)2: the plan is discussed at the start of the year"

#TRACE `the council's two yearly discussions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the pedagogical council` DOES `discuss the plan of action` AT 1
    PARTY `the pedagogical council` DOES `review the execution and its lessons` AT 10

-- ¶123: the council MAY offer its members ways of working, such as the four
-- of ¶124–¶127.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p123
DECLARE `way of working` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p124
    `one or two defined tasks for all teachers for a period, another task after it`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p125
    `a defined task for a group of teachers for the whole year, changing tasks for other groups`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p126
    `tasks by a group of teachers and tasks by single teachers`
    @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p127
    `a defined task coordinated with other institutions in the area`
    `another way of working`

-- ¶128: special attention to the integration and tasks of teachers who are
-- not homeroom teachers — subject teachers and part-timers. ¶129: the team's
-- cohesion and the employees' particular abilities are considered. Both are
-- considerations the council's plan must show it took; they are inputs.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p128 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p129
GIVEN `non-homeroom and part-time teachers are given tasks` IS A BOOLEAN, `team cohesion and abilities were considered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the plan takes the required considerations` `non-homeroom and part-time teachers are given tasks` `team cohesion and abilities were considered` IF
    `non-homeroom and part-time teachers are given tasks` AND `team cohesion and abilities were considered`

-- ¶130: a copy of the council's protocol goes to the institution's
-- supervisor, and its content is discussed at the supervisor's meetings with
-- the principal. The text gives no date, so the duties carry no deadline.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p130
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.17 party` `planning action`
DECIDE `the protocol goes to the supervisor` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the school principal`
    MUST  `send the protocol to the supervisor`
    HENCE (PARTY `a takanon party` `the supervisor`
           MUST  `discuss the protocol with the principal`)

-- ¶131: in kindergartens the work plans are discussed at the kindergarten
-- supervisor's meetings with the kindergarten teachers, by supervision area.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p131
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.17 party` `planning action`
DECIDE `kindergarten plans are discussed` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the supervisor`
    MUST  `discuss the kindergarten plans with the kindergarten teachers`

§§ `1.17.2 ו–ז — principals and supervisors`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p132 Heading: "ו. the stay hours of principals".

-- ¶133: principals use their stay hours to organise and direct the
-- activities above.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p133
DECLARE `principal's stay use` IS ONE OF
    `organising and directing the stay activities`
    `something else`

GIVEN u IS A `principal's stay use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a proper use of a principal's stay hours` u IF
    u EQUALS `organising and directing the stay activities`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p134 Heading: "ז. supervisors".

-- ¶135: supervisors guide and supervise the stay activities.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p135
DECLARE `supervision action` IS ONE OF
    `guide and supervise the stay activities`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `supervision action`
DECIDE `supervising the stay activities` IS
    PARTY `the supervisor`
    MUST  `guide and supervise the stay activities`

-- ¶136: supervisors add 2 weekly hours to their position's hours; ¶137:
-- part-time supervisors work "by section 3 of the agreement" — the agreement's
-- part-time clause, printed here as 1.17.1(2) (see F-1.17-a).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p136 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p137
GIVEN `supervisor's position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a supervisor's weekly stay hours` `supervisor's position share` IS
    IF `supervisor's position share` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `weekly stay hours of a full position`
    ELSE `stay hours up to one position` `supervisor's position share`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p138 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p139 Headings: "2. procedure of scheduling, reporting and follow-up" and "א. general".

-- ¶141: for the scheduling of half stay hours in the timetable of employees
-- in a part-time or an above-full position, "see below, chapter ד', section
-- ה". F-1.17-e: the subsection has no chapter ד'; its lettered parts are א to
-- ז, and ד and ה are the activities of groups and the planning of work. The
-- reading adopted: half-hours are scheduled by 1.17.1 2ד, joined into a whole
-- hour once a fortnight.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p141
GIVEN `weekly stay hours owed` IS A NUMBER @desc of an employee in a part-time or an above-full position
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `half-hours scheduled under the procedure` `weekly stay hours owed` IS
    `stay hours scheduled per fortnight` `weekly stay hours owed`

DECLARE `part of 1.17.2` HAS
    `part letter` IS A STRING
    `part topic`  IS A STRING

`the lettered parts of 1.17.2 as printed` MEANS
    LIST `part of 1.17.2` "א" "general",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ב" "ways to reach the goals",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ג" "the list of activities",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ד" "the activity of groups of teaching employees",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ה" "planning the work",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ו" "the stay hours of principals",
         `part of 1.17.2` "ז" "supervisors"

`"chapter ד' section ה" names no part about half-hours` MEANS
    NOT any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `part topic` EQUALS "scheduling half stay hours")
            `the lettered parts of 1.17.2 as printed`
#ASSERT `"chapter ד' section ה" names no part about half-hours`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p142 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p143 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p144 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p145 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_2/p146 Subsection 1.17.2's source list (אסמכתא): four Director-General's circulars.

§§ `1.17.3 דיווח`

-- 1 ¶1: the principal reports the employees' attendance in the stay hours by
-- the usual reporting arrangements; ¶3: those arrangements and their details
-- are part of the reporting of the employee's attendance in the post. The
-- text names no period: it is the usual one, an input. Time in months.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_1/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_1/p3
GIVEN `the usual reporting period` IS A NUMBER @desc in months, as attendance in the post is reported
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reporting action`
DECIDE `the principal reports stay attendance` `the usual reporting period` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `report attendance in the stay hours`
    WITHIN `the usual reporting period`
    HENCE `the principal reports stay attendance` `the usual reporting period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.17.3(1): the principal reports attendance in the stay hours with the usual reports"

DECLARE `reporting action` IS ONE OF
    `report attendance in the stay hours`
    `report the stay hours in the attendance report`
    `submit a term work plan`
    `submit a term summary report`
    `handle the plan and report as in any subject`
    `record the ongoing stay activity`
    `hand the activity report to the principal for the archive`

-- 1 ¶2: the kindergarten teacher reports her stay hours in the usual
-- attendance report, at its usual period (an input).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_1/p2
GIVEN `the usual reporting period` IS A NUMBER @desc in months, as the attendance report is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reporting action`
DECIDE `the kindergarten teacher reports her stay hours` `the usual reporting period` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `report the stay hours in the attendance report`
    WITHIN `the usual reporting period`
    HENCE `the kindergarten teacher reports her stay hours` `the usual reporting period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.3(1): the kindergarten teacher reports stay hours in the attendance report"

-- 2א: each teacher submits to the principal a work plan for the term
-- ("שליש" or "זמן", as the school does) listing the activities he intends to
-- carry out in the stay hours during it, as in other teaching subjects, based
-- on the institutional plan the council approved; 2ב: at the term's end, a
-- summary report; 2ג: the principal handles both as he does in any other
-- subject. The text sets no date for the plan or for the principal's
-- handling; when the plan is due is the school's practice, an input. Time in
-- months of the term.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_b akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_c
GIVEN `months in the term` IS A NUMBER, `month the school's practice sets for the plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reporting action`
DECIDE `the term's plan and report` `months in the term` `month the school's practice sets for the plan` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `submit a term work plan`
    WITHIN `month the school's practice sets for the plan`
    HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           MUST  `submit a term summary report`
           WITHIN `months in the term`
           HENCE (PARTY `the school principal`
                  MUST  `handle the plan and report as in any subject`)
           LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.3(2)(ב): a summary report at the end of the term")
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.3(2)(א): a work plan for the term"

#TRACE `the term's plan and report` 4 1 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `submit a term work plan` AT 1
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `submit a term summary report` AT 4
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `handle the plan and report as in any subject` AT 5

-- 2ד ¶1: every teaching employee (kindergarten teacher, teacher, principal)
-- records the ongoing activity in the "report of activity in the stay hours
-- in the school year".
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_d/p1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reporting action`
DECIDE `recording the stay activity` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `record the ongoing stay activity`

-- 2ד ¶2: the report stays with the teacher all year and is handed to the
-- principal at the end of the school year, for the institution's archive.
-- School months: the year ends at 12.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_d/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reporting action`
DECIDE `the yearly activity report` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `hand the activity report to the principal for the archive`
    WITHIN `month number` August
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.17.3(2)(ד): the activity report is handed to the principal at the end of the year"

-- 2ה ¶1: supervisors who report on the joint form of attendance and overtime
-- mark (with "ש") the eight stay hours of the month, on top of the overtime
-- approved.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p1
GIVEN `approved overtime hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `joint-form entry`
DECIDE `the joint-form entry` `approved overtime hours` IS
    `joint-form entry` `a supervisor's monthly stay hours` `approved overtime hours`

`a supervisor's monthly stay hours` MEANS 8

DECLARE `joint-form entry` HAS
    `hours marked ש`        IS A NUMBER
    `overtime hours entered` IS A NUMBER

-- 2ה ¶2: the example — a supervisor with 20 approved overtime hours may
-- report 28 hours, as actually worked, and is paid overtime for the 20 only.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p2
GIVEN `approved overtime hours` IS A NUMBER, `hours reported` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `overtime hours paid` `approved overtime hours` `hours reported` IS
    min (`hours reported` MINUS `a supervisor's monthly stay hours`) `approved overtime hours`

`the supervisor example's report` MEANS 20 PLUS `a supervisor's monthly stay hours`
#ASSERT `the supervisor example's report` EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `overtime hours paid` 20 28 EQUALS 20

-- 2ה ¶3: in the report is written "8 ש', 20 שעות נוספות".
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p3
`the example's entry` MEANS `the joint-form entry` 20
#ASSERT `the example's entry`'s `hours marked ש` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the example's entry`'s `overtime hours entered` EQUALS 20

-- 2ה ¶4: supervisors with no overtime approval, or in part-time positions,
-- report on the outside-worker report form, marking "ש" for the stay hours and
-- listing the stay hours beyond their ordinary working hours.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p4
GIVEN `has overtime approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `part-time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `supervisor's report form`
DECIDE `the form the supervisor reports on` `has overtime approval` `part-time` IS
    IF `has overtime approval` AND NOT `part-time`
    THEN `the joint attendance and overtime form`
    ELSE `the outside-worker report form`

DECLARE `supervisor's report form` IS ONE OF
    `the joint attendance and overtime form`
    `the outside-worker report form` @desc the stay hours marked "ש", with the stay hours beyond the ordinary working hours listed

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p7 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3__para_2__subpara_e/p9 A specimen of the yearly activity-report form: its title and blank fields (school, year, teacher's name); the form's table is not in the corpus text.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_3/p2 Subsection 1.17.3's source list (אסמכתא): a Director-General's circular.

§§ `1.17.4 תשלום ותנאים — the stay supplement`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p1 Heading: "1. general".

-- 1א (from 1.6.81): an employee the agreement applies to who stays as above
-- is paid 10% of his combined salary (השכר המשולב), an inseparable part of
-- his salary for every matter, including the allowances and supplements set
-- as a percentage of the combined salary. Dates are YYYYMMDD.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p3
GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `stays as the agreement requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stay supplement` `month as a date` `combined salary` `stays as the agreement requires` IS
    IF `stays as the agreement requires` AND `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 June 1981`
    THEN `combined salary` TIMES `the stay supplement rate`
    ELSE 0

`the stay supplement rate` MEANS 10%
`1 June 1981`    MEANS 19810601

-- Part of the salary "for every matter": the base on which percentage
-- allowances are computed includes it.
GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the base of percentage allowances` `month as a date` `combined salary` IS
    `combined salary` PLUS `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` `month as a date` `combined salary` TRUE

-- The employer's duty to pay it, as part of the salary.
GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `payment action`
DECIDE `paying the stay supplement` `month as a date` `combined salary` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the stay supplement` x
          PROVIDED x AT LEAST `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` `month as a date` `combined salary` TRUE
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.17.4(1)(א): 10% of the combined salary is paid for the stay hours"

DECLARE `payment action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the stay supplement` HAS `amount of the supplement` IS A NUMBER

#TRACE `paying the stay supplement` 19900101 10000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the stay supplement` 1000 AT 1

#ASSERT `the stay supplement` 19900101 10000 TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the base of percentage allowances` 19900101 10000 EQUALS 11000

-- From 1.1.94 the stay supplement is included in the combined-salary tables:
-- from then on it is in the combined salary, not paid on top of it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p5
GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the combined-salary tables include the stay supplement` `month as a date` IF
    `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 January 1994`

`1 January 1994` MEANS 19940101

GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `stays as the agreement requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` `month as a date` `combined salary` `stays as the agreement requires` IS
    IF `the combined-salary tables include the stay supplement` `month as a date`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the stay supplement` `month as a date` `combined salary` `stays as the agreement requires`

#ASSERT `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` 19900101 10000 TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` 19950101 10000 TRUE EQUALS 0

-- 1ב: on paid leave, reserve duty, sick leave and the like, with the proper
-- confirmations, the employee is entitled to the 10% for that period; 1ג:
-- one who received it before the official vacations gets it for the vacation
-- too.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p7
DECLARE `kind of absence` IS ONE OF
    `paid leave`
    `reserve duty`
    `sick leave`
    `a similar absence`
    `an official vacation of the education system`
    `another absence`

GIVEN a IS A `kind of absence`, `brought confirmations` IS A BOOLEAN, `received it before the vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement is paid for the absence` a `brought confirmations` `received it before the vacation` IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `an official vacation of the education system` THEN `received it before the vacation`
    WHEN `another absence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `brought confirmations`

-- 1ד: "the application of sections 1 and 2 is from 1 September 1981".
-- F-1.17-f: read as this subsection's own 1 and 2 (the payment, and the
-- conditions), it contradicts 1א's "from 1.6.81" and 2ב's "from 1.6.1981".
-- The reading adopted: it dates 1ב and 1ג — the clauses it closes and shares
-- the footnote (6) with — from 1.9.81, and 1א keeps 1.6.81.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p8
`1 September 1981` MEANS 19810901

GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence and vacation rules apply` `month as a date` IF
    `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 September 1981`

`"sections 1 and 2 from 1.9.81" contradicts the start dates the sections give themselves` MEANS
        NOT `1 September 1981` EQUALS `1 June 1981`
    AND `the stay supplement paid on top of the tables` 19810701 10000 TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `"sections 1 and 2 from 1.9.81" contradicts the start dates the sections give themselves`

§§ `1.17.4 2 — pension, unpaid leave and severance`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p9 Heading: "2. conditions".

-- 2א ¶1: the payment enters the determining salary for pension of employees
-- who retire after the agreement was signed and were entitled to it on the
-- eve of retirement, by the existing rules on computing the pension. ¶2: it
-- applies also to pensioners who retired before 1.6.81, from 1.10.82.
-- 2ב.5: one who bought pension rights for unpaid leave and retired at its
-- end counts as entitled on the eve of retirement.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p10 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p11 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p20
`1 October 1982` MEANS 19821001

GIVEN `retired before 1.6.81` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled on the eve of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `bought rights for unpaid leave and retired at its end` IS A BOOLEAN, `pension month as a date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement enters the determining salary for pension` `retired before 1.6.81` `entitled on the eve of retirement` `bought rights for unpaid leave and retired at its end` `pension month as a date` IF
    IF `retired before 1.6.81`
    THEN `pension month as a date` AT LEAST `1 October 1982`
    ELSE `entitled on the eve of retirement` OR `bought rights for unpaid leave and retired at its end`

-- 2ב: the parity committee's conclusions on unpaid leave. Its recitals
-- (¶13–¶15) say why: an employee on unpaid leave may buy pension rights
-- under Takshir 33.46 by paying 18.5% monthly of the salary that would have
-- been due, and the stay supplement is part of that salary. ¶16: the recitals
-- are part of the conclusions. ¶17: the supplement is included in that
-- salary. ¶18: also for leave that began before 1.6.1981, from that date.
-- ¶21: the conclusions apply from 1.6.1981.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p12 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p13 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p14 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p21
`the pension-rights payment rate` MEANS 18.5%

GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `salary that would have been due without the supplement` IS A NUMBER, `stay supplement that would have been due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary for the pension-rights payment` `month as a date` `salary that would have been due without the supplement` `stay supplement that would have been due` IS
    IF `month as a date` AT LEAST `1 June 1981`
    THEN `salary that would have been due without the supplement` PLUS `stay supplement that would have been due`
    ELSE `salary that would have been due without the supplement`

GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `salary that would have been due without the supplement` IS A NUMBER, `stay supplement that would have been due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly payment for pension rights on unpaid leave` `month as a date` `salary that would have been due without the supplement` `stay supplement that would have been due` IS
    `the pension-rights payment rate` TIMES `the salary for the pension-rights payment` `month as a date` `salary that would have been due without the supplement` `stay supplement that would have been due`

#ASSERT `the monthly payment for pension rights on unpaid leave` 19820101 10000 1000 EQUALS 2035

-- ¶19: where the unpaid leave was approved on condition of paying 5% of the
-- salary that would have been due, that salary too includes the supplement
-- from 1.6.1981.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p19
`the leave-condition payment rate` MEANS 5%

GIVEN `month as a date` IS A NUMBER, `salary that would have been due without the supplement` IS A NUMBER, `stay supplement that would have been due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly 5% leave-condition payment` `month as a date` `salary that would have been due without the supplement` `stay supplement that would have been due` IS
    `the leave-condition payment rate` TIMES `the salary for the pension-rights payment` `month as a date` `salary that would have been due without the supplement` `stay supplement that would have been due`

-- 2ג: a teacher entitled to the supplement on 1.6.81 and dismissed after that
-- date has it included in the base for severance pay.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p22
GIVEN `entitled on 1.6.81` IS A BOOLEAN, `dismissal date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplement enters the severance base` `entitled on 1.6.81` `dismissal date` IF
    `entitled on 1.6.81` AND `dismissal date` GREATER THAN `1 June 1981`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p23 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p25 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p26 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p27 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p28 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p29 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_17__ssec_1_17_4/p30 Subsection 1.17.4's source list (אסמכתא): a government decision, circulars, the 1994 agreements, a special agreement of 30.1.83 and a letter of 30.11.81.
